Below is a brief of what’s going wrong and how we fix it, then the actual *SEARCH/REPLACE* patches for both files.

1) Bug Scenario & Root Cause  
   In CSS you can write:  
     ```css
     @import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;500;600;700&display=swap');
     ```  
   Prism’s CSS‐lang plugin is supposed to treat the entire `'…swap'` as one string inside the `url()`, but because of a subtle regex-grouping mistake the engine stops at the first `:` or `;` and falls back to other tokenizers (punctuation, etc.). In short, the alternation around `string.source` in the `url()` pattern isn’t properly grouped, nor is the “inside” string pattern fully anchored, so only the first chunk (`'https`) ends up as a string token.

2) The Fix  
   Wrap `string.source` in its own non-capturing group both in the outer `url` pattern and in the inner `string` pattern. That restores proper alternation precedence and ensures the entire quoted URL is consumed as one string.

